          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "My doctor says I have type 2 diabetes.",
          "answer": "I'm sorry to hear that. Receiving a diagnosis can bring a lot of questions, so here is what the reference material I searched says.\n\n**What type 2 diabetes is.** According to the General clinical reference \"Type 2 diabetes mellitus,\" it is a condition where the body's tissues respond poorly to insulin, and the pancreas cannot keep up with the extra insulin needed. This leaves blood sugar above the normal range. It develops gradually over years, and many people have no symptoms at diagnosis.\n\n**Lifestyle points.** The National diabetes association nutrition guidance says that where body weight is above the healthy range, weight reduction can improve blood sugar, blood pressure and cholesterol. It notes that a sustained five percent reduction gives measurable benefit. It also says \"sugar-free\" does not mean \"carbohydrate-free,\" and that whole fruit is still part of recommended eating. The source says diet targets should be set with your own clinician.\n\n**Emergency signs.** The Diabetes association and emergency medicine guidance says very high blood sugar can be dangerous. Call emergency services immediately if you have nausea, vomiting or belly pain, deep or fast breathing or breath with a fruity smell, drowsiness or confusion, severe dehydration, or you cannot pass urine or keep fluids down.\n\n**What these sources did not cover.** I could not find guidance in these results on treatment choices, medicines, blood sugar targets, or what your own test results mean. Those decisions depend on your personal health, so please bring them to your doctor. Useful questions include: What type of diabetes testing did I have? What is my next step? Do I need a plan for low or high blood sugar? Are there foods, activity, or weight goals that suit me?\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
