          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How often should it be checked?",
          "answer": "The reference material I searched gives a general schedule for HbA1c, a blood test that shows average blood sugar over about three months. According to the National diabetes association standards of care summary (\"Type 2 diabetes: glycemic targets and monitoring intervals\"), HbA1c is checked:\n\n- **At least twice a year** for people who are meeting their blood sugar goal on a stable treatment plan.\n- **Every three months** for people who are not yet at their goal, or whose treatment has recently changed.\n\nThe same passage does not say how often you should check your blood sugar at home, or how often other tests should be done. Your own schedule depends on your treatment, your results and your health history, so ask your doctor: \"How often should I have my HbA1c checked, and do I need to check my blood sugar at home?\"\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
